⚠️ Risks & Considerations
Learning Curve: Spring’s vast ecosystem can be overwhelming for beginners.

Configuration Complexity: Traditional Spring projects may require extensive XML/Java configuration (though Spring Boot reduces this).

Performance Overhead: Improper use of DI or AOP can lead to inefficiencies.

✅ In summary: Spring’s features make it the go-to framework for modern Java development, especially for enterprise-scale, cloud-native, and microservice architectures. Its modularity, productivity tools (like Spring Boot), and strong community support ensure it remains highly relevant in 2026.
